{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1073315-dismemberment-and-vampiric-healing","id":1073315,"title":"Dismemberment and vampiric healing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-04T12:54:04-07:00","id":1073315,"title":"Dismemberment and vampiric healing","content":"I'm curious about how you guys deal with the healing factor of the vampiric condition. Now I'm aware that there are the official rules and such, but as I read through <i>&quot;The Vampire Chroicles&quot;</i> book series, I found it interesting that while vampires heal, they do not regenerate lost limbs. Eyes, hans, tongues etc - if they're lost, they're lost until you manage to physically retrieve them. You can however replace them with human limbs for a while. And while I, as a Storyteller (and as a player, really, but I often differ from those around me), can see the potential in this for story hooks, personal drama and combat complexities, I find myself wondering what other people think.<br /> <br /> Would you guys try the <i>&quot;Vampire Chronicles&quot; </i>method where you can heal your wounds and damage, yet lost limbs remain lost, or would you prefer to have the limbs regrow? And what is your reasons for this decision? (I'm interested in both the Player and Storyteller perspective) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T14:12:41-07:00","id":1073354,"title":"","content":"We always play in the way the limbs can regrow. A lost limb due to lethal damage wouldn't be a huge issue, since you can heal it straight away if you have enough blood and the masquerade isn't a problem. Aggravated damage heals in a more difficult way (for instance claws of the unholy attack to the arm). Healing a 3A wound is difficult enough, but if you want to make it even more complex feel free, but you should remember that in mixed chronicles the undead will be weaker in comparison to the living, since they lost their ability. <br /> I'm curious what others think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T15:18:48-07:00","id":1073394,"title":"","content":"Honestly I prefer vampires regrowing their limbs. It highlights their bestial side as only (some) animals can regrow lost limbs whereas requiring them to have them surgically or prosthetically replaced makes them more human or serves as a means to justify the act of mutilating someone else or defiling a deceased person in order to be made &quot;whole&quot; again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T17:20:49-07:00","id":1073445,"title":"","content":"For personal stories, playing find the foot or chase the one-armed man can be fun. But it either needs to wrap up or the players need to except lose. <br /> Limb regrowth is an easier answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}